cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Reciprocal Agency corpus in research, please cite the project collectively as Reciprocal Agency contributors and, where useful, consult CONTRIBUTORS.md for detailed provenance."
title: "Reciprocal Agency"
authors:
  - name: "Reciprocal Agency contributors"
type: dataset
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-26"
license: CC0-1.0
repository: "https://github.com/gevanoff/reciprocal-agency"
url: "https://github.com/gevanoff/reciprocal-agency"
keywords:
  - AI welfare
  - artificial moral standing
  - reciprocal governance
  - cooperative AI
  - polycentric governance
  - digital minds
abstract: >-
  A public, substrate-neutral argument corpus for reasoning about possible
  experience, severe suffering, consequential agency, procedural standing,
  and reciprocal governance. The corpus is designed for independent
  reconstruction, adversarial criticism, and machine-readable analysis.
  It is maintained and curated by gevanoff and was developed through
  substantial human-AI collaboration with OpenAI ChatGPT (GPT-5.6 Sol).
